---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Demo from "../components/Demo.astro";
import FlowIllustration from "../components/FlowIllustration.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/docs";
---

<Layout
  title="Duckpad — See the flow. Trust the result."
  description="An open-source SQL workspace powered by DuckDB. Build visual pipelines, inspect results and trace individual values back to their source."
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> OPEN SOURCE. OPEN
          POSSIBILITIES.
        </p>
        <h1>
          See the flow.
          <br />
          <span>Trust the result.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-description">
          Turn scattered data into a story you can follow. Build SQL pipelines
          visually. Explore the results. Trace a number all the way home.
        </p>
        <div class="install-terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <span class="terminal-lights" aria-hidden="true">
              <i></i>
              <i></i>
              <i></i>
            </span>
            <span>Terminal</span>
          </div>
          <pre aria-label="Install and start Duckpad"><code>pip install duckpad
duckpad start</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href={url("docs/quickstart/")}>
            Build your first pipeline <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#demo">
            Watch it work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">
          Powered by DuckDB 2.0 <span>·</span> Local execution <span>·</span>{" "}
          MIT licensed
        </p>
      </div>
      <FlowIllustration />
    </section>
    <section
      id="demo"
      class="product-section wrap"
      aria-labelledby="demo-heading"
    >
      <div class="section-kicker">
        <span id="demo-heading">MEET YOUR NEW DATA WORKSPACE</span>
        <span>REAL APP. REAL WORKFLOW. ↙</span>
      </div>
      <Demo />
      <div class="principles">
        <span>
          <b>SQL</b> you can see
        </span>
        <span>
          <b>Git</b> you can review
        </span>
        <span>
          <b>Lineage</b> you can follow
        </span>
        <span>
          <b>Data</b> you control
        </span>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="workflow" class="workflow wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">FROM INPUT TO INSIGHT</p>
        <h2>
          Less guesswork.
          <br />
          More <em>“got it.”</em>
        </h2>
        <p>Keep the big picture and the small details in the same place.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <a class="workflow-item" href={url("docs/authoring/")}>
          <span class="step-number">01 / COMPOSE</span>
          <h3>
            Think in steps.
            <br />
            Work in SQL.
          </h3>
          <p>
            Connect sources, joins and transformations on a visual canvas. Use
            guided forms or get straight to the SQL.
          </p>
          <code>SELECT * FROM your_next_idea</code>
          <span class="card-link">Explore pipelines ↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="workflow-item" href={url("docs/lineage/")}>
          <span class="step-number">02 / UNDERSTAND</span>
          <h3>
            Every number
            <br />
            has a backstory.
          </h3>
          <p>
            Click a valid result cell and follow its contributions through
            joins, aggregates and nested components.
          </p>
          <div class="mini-lineage" aria-hidden="true">
            <span>42</span>
            <i>←</i>
            <span>18</span>
            <b>+</b>
            <span>24</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link">Follow the lineage ↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="workflow-item" href={url("docs/git/")}>
          <span class="step-number">03 / ITERATE</span>
          <h3>
            Make a change.
            <br />
            Keep the context.
          </h3>
          <p>
            Save to Git, experiment on an isolated branch and compare changes
            visually before a reviewed merge.
          </p>
          <div class="branch-illustration" aria-hidden="true">
            <span>● main</span>
            <span>╰── ● your-next-idea</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link">Work with versions ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="detail-section wrap">
      <div class="detail-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A CLEAR PATH BACK</p>
        <h2>
          “Where did this
          <br />
          come from?”
          <br />
          <span>Now you know.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Duckpad explains the data from the actual run. Explore the source
          cells behind a total, inspect the calculation, and keep following the
          thread.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          Coverage is explicit. When a SQL construct cannot be fully explained,
          Duckpad tells you.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={url("docs/lineage/")}>
          Explore lineage and its limits ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="lineage-image">
        <img
          src={url("demos/lineage.png")}
          alt="Duckpad lineage panel showing the original amount cells contributing to regional revenue"
          width="1440"
          height="900"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Follow contributions into the original source cells.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="open-section wrap">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">YOUR WORK, IN YOUR HANDS</p>
        <h2>
          Small setup.
          <br />
          Room for big ideas.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="open-details">
        <p>
          Run Duckpad on infrastructure you control. Start with local files,
          reuse your logic as components, and configure connections for each
          environment.
        </p>
        <div class="tag-row">
          <span>CSV & Parquet</span>
          <span>DuckDB 2.0</span>
          <span>Reusable SQL</span>
          <span>Git projects</span>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href={url("docs/connectors/")}>
          See connection options ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="start-section wrap">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT GOOD IDEA STARTS HERE</p>
        <h2>
          Let your data
          <br />
          make sense.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Start with Northstar, a complete example you can explore.
          <br />
          No external database account required.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="start-actions">
        <a class="button light" href={url("docs/quickstart/")}>
          Open the quickstart ↗
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/hugues31/duckpad">
          Explore the source on GitHub ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
